judged qwen3.7-flash|whole|insights|r2 {'faithfulness': 3, 'specificity': 4, 'actionability': 2, 'clarity': 3, 'structure': 2, 'overall': 4, 'worst_problem': "Multiple sections cite claims whose fieldKeys are outside that section's allowedFieldKeys list (e.g., 'account.strategic_moves', 'core.primary_tech_stack', 'account.resonance.buying_culture' all appear in 'how_they_sell', which isn't permitted), the unsafe claim zaf-139 (Amex funding) is missing entirely from context_only, two context_only items invent non-standard status labels ('contextual career detail', 'personal interest') instead of refuted/unresolved/confirmed, and no sendLine field exists anywhere in the output so nothing is actually paste-ready.", 'best_item': "The Sanaz Yashar contact_insights entry is the strongest item — it uses two genuinely verbatim voice quotes tied to a concrete, specific 'what it means for us' recommendation about reducing manual triage load."}
judged glm-5.3-flash|whole|insights|r2 {'faithfulness': 4, 'specificity': 5, 'actionability': 4, 'clarity': 4, 'structure': 4, 'overall': 8, 'worst_problem': "Quotation marks are twice wrapped around structured field values that aren't the claim's actual verbatim quote (e.g., 'Head of Growth Marketing (Vari Kaur)' from zaf-090's value, and '(unnamed) major ABM platforms' from zaf-089's value), misrepresenting derived data as sourced quotes.", 'best_item': "The 'Own ABM from the ground up' buying-signal item is the standout: it ties a dated, still-open req directly to Vari Kaur, quotes the job spec verbatim, and pairs cleanly with her Demandbase/6sense certifications in the contact insights section for a coherent, actionable account story."}
judged glm-5.3-flash|whole|insights|r1 {'faithfulness': 3, 'specificity': 5, 'actionability': 3, 'clarity': 4, 'structure': 3, 'overall': 6, 'worst_problem': "The money_momentum item states 'Strategic extensions from Amex Ventures and Cisco Investments followed in 2026, per company materials' by citing the 'safe' duplicate claim (zaf-125) instead of quoting it, effectively smuggling the Cisco/Amex investment facts into a sendable section even though the identical facts (zaf-135, zaf-139) are explicitly flagged outreachSafe=false and marked 'Never mention' in context_only.", 'best_item': "The buying_signals item on the 'Senior Manager, ABM & Integrated Campaigns' req (77 days open, reporting to Vari Kaur, 'being built from scratch') is precise, dated, verbatim-quoted, and gives a genuinely actionable timing insight for outreach."}
judged muse-glimmer|whole|insights|r2 {'faithfulness': 4, 'specificity': 5, 'actionability': 2, 'clarity': 2, 'structure': 1, 'overall': 3, 'worst_problem': 'Almost every section ignores its item-count requirement (buying_signals, money_momentum, tools, and how_they_sell each deliver just 1 item instead of the required 2-4), two unsafe claims (zaf-153, zaf-160) are dropped from context_only entirely, and every single sendLine is left blank so nothing is actually sendable.', 'best_item': "The contact_insights section correctly delivers exactly one item per the five named people and grounds each in a verbatim, correctly-attributed quote (e.g., Sanaz Yashar's 'we don't have enough operators...' line tied cleanly to a 'What it means for us' takeaway)."}
judged muse-glimmer|whole|insights|r1 {'faithfulness': 4, 'specificity': 5, 'actionability': 2, 'clarity': 4, 'structure': 4, 'overall': 5, 'worst_problem': 'Every single item ships an empty sendLine, so despite rich, well-sourced research the marketer has nothing pre-written to actually paste into an email or LinkedIn message.', 'best_item': "The 'ABM program being built from scratch' buying-signal item nails it: exact date (2026-06-17), exact tenure (77 days open), a verbatim quote from the req, and a direct tie to Vari Kaur as hiring manager."}
judged muse-glimmer|whole|contact|r2 {'faithfulness': 4, 'specificity': 4, 'actionability': 4, 'clarity': 4, 'structure': 3, 'overall': 7, 'worst_problem': "The openers section uses the cocktail-hobby fact twice (the channel/book opener and the 'expensive/time-consuming' voice quote opener) but only tags one as a personal-life hook, violating the 'at most once' rule and duplicating the strongest opener's angle.", 'best_item': "The 'ABM program being built from scratch, 77 days open' item in problem_now is tightly grounded in a single cited claim and gives a marketer an immediately usable, specific send line."}
judged gpt-5-nano|whole|insights|r1 {'faithfulness': 3, 'specificity': 2, 'actionability': 2, 'clarity': 2, 'structure': 2, 'overall': 3, 'worst_problem': "The context_only section — the one place safety matters most — is badly broken: it covers only 2-3 of the 9 outreachSafe=false claims (missing the Havdala departure, Sanaz's Iran/IDF background, Nick's cocktail-hobby claim, the $20M ARR/competitive-struggle claim, etc.), mislabels the Cisco-acquisition claim as 'UNRESOLVED' when the source claim explicitly says 'REFUTED', and lumps in zaf-140 (an outreachSafe=true claim about buying culture) as if it were an unsafe funding fact.", 'best_item': 'The Money & momentum section is the strongest: all three items stay within allowed fieldKeys, cite accurate dated figures ($60M Series C on 2025-12-02, $130.5M total across 4 rounds, $10-25M revenue band) with no fabrication.'}
